ence suggests either is likely.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Open seat: Dusty Johnson (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Dusty Johnson's retirement to run for governor leaves an open seat in a heavily Republican state, and Republicans nominated well-known former attorney general Marty Jackley. Jackley has raised about $1.4 million and holds over $1 million on hand, while Democrat Nikki Gronli has raised roughly $260,000 with modest cash reserves and no reported outside support.\n\nThe district's R+15 lean, the fundraising gap, and prediction markets pricing Gronli's chances near 4% all point the same direction. A single Democratic-sponsored poll from late August shows Jackley up four points, likely understating his true advantage in this environment. The forecast treats this as a safe Republican hold, with Gronli needing an extraordinary shift to compete.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -15.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0242, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0239, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.019, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0299, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0301, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0189, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0348, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.036